1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
Farmers can walk a field,
but they cannot see red-edge,

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,000
near-infrared,
or short-wave infrared.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,500
Sentinel-2 captures those signals, yet turning
a season of satellite data

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:15,800
into a useful field visit usually requires
specialist software.

5
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:18,000
1415 Agri makes that workflow accessible.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,200
This is a Collaborative Partner,
not a diagnostic chatbot.

7
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:28,800
Gemini 3.5 Flash leads the workflow
through Google ADK and MCP tools.

8
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:34,000
Deterministic services measure the pixels;
the farmer confirms the boundary and decides what to inspect.

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:39,000
This family field in Taquarituba
is authorized for this demonstration.

10
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,500
We provide soybeans, the 2025–26 season,
36 hectares, and a reference point.

11
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:49,500
Guided mode is off, so every result comes
from the real satellite workflow

12
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:55,000
now reaching Django on Cloud Run,
with a traceable request ID for replay and auditing.

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The proposed polygon is never accepted silently.

14
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
The service suggests a boundary around the reference
point, but the farmer stays in control.

15
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,500
I can inspect the outline, correct a point,
compare its 30.3-hectare estimate with the expected area,

16
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:15,000
and explicitly confirm the cultivated area
before analysis can start.

17
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,800
Cloud Tasks now delivers an authenticated job
to a private Cloud Run worker.

18
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:24,500
It searches real Sentinel-2 Level-2A observations,
reads bounded image windows,

19
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:29,000
applies cloud masking,
aligns the dates,

20
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,200
and calculates NDVI, NDRE, and NDMI.

21
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:38,000
In this live run, the worker selects five usable observations
from October through March

22
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,500
and completes the analysis in 93 seconds.

23
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:47,000
Progress and provenance are persisted at every stage.

24
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,500
The same analysis ID ties every stage together.
These are checkpoints from the live processing run.

25
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:55,000
Gemini does not calculate or invent these pixels;
it reasons only after deterministic processing is complete.

26
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
The output divides one field into four areas
with different spectral trajectories.

27
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,500
We compare five usable Sentinel-2 observations
and inspect every value behind the map.

28
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:11,000
Evidence stays connected to dates,
NDVI, NDRE, NDMI, mission metadata,

29
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:16,000
source bands, cloud coverage, and provenance.
Area One differs most clearly.

30
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:22,000
This is a scouting priority map,
not a diagnosis.

31
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Gemini receives typed evidence, not raw rasters.

32
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Asked where to scout first, it selects Area One,
compares February twenty-second and March fourteenth,

33
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:36,000
cites NDVI, NDRE, and NDMI,
and returns three field steps without diagnosis.

34
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:41,000
The table is the field-wide baseline;
the cited values are persisted Area One observations

35
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:45,000
from get_analysis_evidence.
The trace exposes Gemini 3.5 Flash,

36
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Google ADK, the temporal specialist, and MCP tools,
so the chain remains auditable.

37
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:57,500
This second turn changes application state.

38
00:02:57,500 --> 00:03:03,000
With explicit permission, the temporal specialist
calls request_field_analysis,

39
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:09,000
creates a three-area comparison, and queues work.
The returned analysis ID connects it to worker logs,

40
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:15,000
while idempotency prevents a Gemini retry from creating
duplicate jobs and preserves an audit trail.

41
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:19,500
The farmer can request a different grouping
and rate the explanation.

42
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:23,500
Feedback is stored with the exact analysis
and conversation;

43
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:27,000
it never silently changes
the scientific result.

44
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:31,500
One immutable container runs as four separately
permissioned Cloud Run services.

45
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:34,800
Vertex AI provides Gemini;

46
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:38,200
Firestore stores evidence and feedback;

47
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:41,500
Cloud Storage stores artifacts;
and Cloud Tasks runs the satellite workflow.

48
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:44,000
Private endpoints reject anonymous calls.

49
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:49,000
1415 Agri turns invisible satellite signals
into an understandable, accountable field visit

50
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:53,000
for farmers left out
of precision agriculture.
